{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Balaam lifted up his eyes.</b> He sought to cast an evil eye upon them — and behold, you have three of his traits: an evil eye, a haughty spirit, and a broad soul, as stated above." "<b>Each tribe by its tribes.</b> He saw each and every tribe dwelling on its own, not intermingled. He saw that their openings were not aligned one opposite the other, so that no one would peer into the tent of his fellow." "<b>And the spirit of Elohim came upon him.</b> It entered his heart not to curse them."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:30.441231482Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}